# Defense-in-depth response headers for every Community page. Mirrors
# marketing's public/_headers: the community app is static assets only (no
# worker), so the headers go through Cloudflare Workers Static Assets'
# `_headers` file, which Next.js copies from public/ into out/ at build time.
# Paths are as the assets worker sees them, after the router strips
# `/community`.
#
# X-Frame-Options DENY matters most here: signed-in visitors can Like, Report
# and Copy, so a framed page could be clickjacked into doing those.
# `fullscreen` is left out of Permissions-Policy because a post page embeds
# the live editor, which may go fullscreen.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
